      "subject": "הרעים הרעים",
      "rationale": "The participle is doubled — 'the shepherds, the shepherds' — an emphatic repetition flattened to 'the ones shepherding' in English."
    },
    {
      "kind": "you",
      "subject": "to the shepherds",
      "rationale": "YHWH's indictment addresses the shepherds of Israel directly in the second person."
    }
  ],
  "translation": "Therefore thus said YHWH, Elohim of Israel, against the shepherds, the ones shepherding ⟨את⟩ my people: you are the ones who scattered ⟨את⟩ my flock and drove them away, and did not attend to ⟨את⟩ them. Behold me, attending upon you ⟨את⟩ the evil of your doings — oracle of YHWH.",
